// [Event Declarations.note]            search in ssTEA source files for a reference to this file.
//
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The ssTEA Event Declarations note explains the compiler language terms used to implement ssTEA.
   The ssTEA Event Agency note explains Event activities as they are implemented using the terms.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   These are states used by ssTEA to describe Events; the Agency Run FSM will be in one of these.
   These are probably not states that a USER's FSM Events will go through as the USER's FSM runs;
   state changes in user FSMs are only possible while the Agency Run FSM is in "agencying" state.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
typedef enum ssA_Runfsm_State_e
//
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   when an event is run (the function pointed to is called by AgencyRoot), it owns the mesa.
   when an event runs and encounters non-normal events that require the event by halted: return reset.
   when an event runs and has no errors occur regardless of operations performed: return Normal.
   when some piece of ssTEA services fail to work as described: return Flaw.
   the Event function return value signals to ssTEA : this event ran as normal, or, a reset is occuring.
   In all cases, the result value returned is stored in the Event agency User data structure.
   ssTEA does not refer to any value that is beyond the declared range, storing it in the User agency
   data structure for reference by the User who wants to know why they signaled an error to ssTEA.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
typedef enum ssE_EvResult_e
//
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   These counters are used to track Agency grants and the action taken after Agency is given up.
   The counters are related to the operations of the Event Agency Run FSM as ssA's agency controller.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The App's Event data is available during the Event, a pointer is provided when Agency is granted.
   When the pointer is stored in the About Event data by the App, it is typecast: "pointer to void".
   The canonical parameter definition for an Event includes "a pointer to void": the App's pointer.
   This is typecast in the Event to the App's definition of the data, so the App code sees its data.
   ssTEA does not access the actual value of the field, except when granting Agency to the Event.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   It would be nice to avoid the transition through "pointer to void", but the dependency of ssTEA
   for the App Data definition would require the definition precede ssTEA to be referenced by ssTEA.
   This also would in precede the definition by ssTEA of useful ssTEA types such as Time Variables.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   typedef pVoid_t                 EvEx_App_pEventData_t

// S~S  SimpleSal signal ends  S~S
